This depends on what your definition of "best" is.

If the benefit of the other cloaks when not standing next to water is
insignificant, and the benefit of the oilskin cloak when standing next
to water is very significant (potentially lifesaving), and the odds
that you won't switch cloaks when going next to water are non-
negligible, then the oilskin cloak may very well give you the best
odds of ascending.

IMO, once you're past the early game and are tanked up, there's almost
no measurable impact of displacement on ascension percentage (and if
anything, it would likely be negative given displacement's ability to
mess up Elbereth and make monsters attack more randomly, threatening
pets and strategy).  Unless you're lacking stealth otherwise,
oilskin's a clear win.  If you are, it's a closer call.

At any rate, all of those options pale in comparison to the better
cloaks.  And this is very different from the early game-when you're
not tanked up, displacement is a big plus.

